.\" - Pete Hegseth", "last_comment_created": 1794009369132, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 7, "score_up": 25, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 0, "created": 1793993270000, "id": "2118787462696743035", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1892730921830223873/FnaA9xYs_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Pete Hegseth", "username": "PeteHegseth"}, "content": "Patriots in control.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 68194}, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 201, "created": 1793996862000, "id": "2118802526535622742", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1463062461934931969/2VtwipQQ_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Clandestine", "username": "WarClandestine"}, "content": "You guys can\u2019t get mad at me for pointing it out. It\u2019s coming directly from the top.\n\nIf you think the Trump administration and the Secretary of War don\u2019t know what this means, you are mistaken.\n\nThey know EXACTLY what they are doing.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 7975}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToZ25lWS", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 40, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8927360, "raw_content": "Hey family, Ryan here\n\n\n Hope you\u2019re all doing well. These midterms have been stirring something deeper in me. I keep coming back to the same thought: we may be missing something important. We\u2019ve become far too dependent on the political system to be our savior. It\u2019s easy to hide behind anonymous accounts, talk a strong game, and then wait for someone else to actually take the risk and walk it out.\n\n The disciples saw Jesus moving so powerfully that they were willing to die for it. Yet so often we sit back and wait for someone else to come save the day.\n\n What if Trump isn\u2019t the one who saves us? What if, like John the Baptist, he was simply a messenger clearing the way for something much larger? A movement that rises above politics and comes together as a real, public body in the world\u2014not just online.\n\n I know I\u2019m not the sharpest person here, and many of you have poured yourselves into the digital work of holding this community together. But very little of what we talk about seems to turn into real-world action. It often stays at digital decodes that lead us to keep waiting\u2026 and waiting\u2026 and waiting.\n\n I don\u2019t always know the best way to say what I feel needs to be said. But I do know this: for any lasting change to happen, this has to become about Jesus. Not politics. Not America. Not even primarily about taking down the deep state. Those things matter and play a part, but we have to remember that a united body of believers standing in truth and humble prayer is where real change actually begins.\nI\u2019ve been using my home state of Delaware as a kind of launch point for the vision the Lord has given me. After talking with people from all walks of life, I can say without hesitation that Jesus is preparing hearts and minds to unite around prayer and seeking Him. As I\u2019ve been building in Delaware, the Lord has also shown me that .win\u2014and each of you\u2014have a role to play in this.\n\n Please pray over what I\u2019m saying. Let\u2019s start talking about real-world action. I\u2019m willing to stand up where needed and put myself out there, but each of you carries a part that I simply can\u2019t do for you. I can be a messenger, but I can\u2019t force anyone to move. I believe the Lord has given me a vision that ties all of this together, and I\u2019ve been patiently waiting for each of you to be activated.\n\n Love you all. I appreciate everything you do, and I\u2019m grateful to walk this journey with you.\n\n ***Together through Christ  we have endless potential.***", "author": "Slechta5614", "created": 1793996188988, "profile_picture": "VFq5QWknnyxv", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Slechta5614", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "\ud83d\ude4fLord reveal your will to .WIN\ud83d\ude4f", "last_comment_created": 1794008895671, "content": "<p>Hey family, Ryan here</p>\n<p>Hope you\u2019re all doing well. These midterms have been stirring something deeper in me. I keep coming back to the same thought: we may be missing something important. We\u2019ve become far too dependent on the political system to be our savior. It\u2019s easy to hide behind anonymous accounts, talk a strong game, and then wait for someone else to actually take the risk and walk it out.</p>\n<p>The disciples saw Jesus moving so powerfully that they were willing to die for it. Yet so often we sit back and wait for someone else to come save the day.</p>\n<p>What if Trump isn\u2019t the one who saves us? What if, like John the Baptist, he was simply a messenger clearing the way for something much larger? A movement that rises above politics and comes together as a real, public body in the world\u2014not just online.</p>\n<p>I know I\u2019m not the sharpest person here, and many of you have poured yourselves into the digital work of holding this community together. But very little of what we talk about seems to turn into real-world action. It often stays at digital decodes that lead us to keep waiting\u2026 and waiting\u2026 and waiting.</p>\n<p>I don\u2019t always know the best way to say what I feel needs to be said. But I do know this: for any lasting change to happen, this has to become about Jesus. Not politics. Not America. Not even primarily about taking down the deep state. Those things matter and play a part, but we have to remember that a united body of believers standing in truth and humble prayer is where real change actually begins.\nI\u2019ve been using my home state of Delaware as a kind of launch point for the vision the Lord has given me. After talking with people from all walks of life, I can say without hesitation that Jesus is preparing hearts and minds to unite around prayer and seeking Him. As I\u2019ve been building in Delaware, the Lord has also shown me that .win\u2014and each of you\u2014have a role to play in this.</p>\n<p>Please pray over what I\u2019m saying. Let\u2019s start talking about real-world action. I\u2019m willing to stand up where needed and put myself out there, but each of you carries a part that I simply can\u2019t do for you. I can be a messenger, but I can\u2019t force anyone to move. I believe the Lord has given me a vision that ties all of this together, and I\u2019ve been patiently waiting for each of you to be activated.</p>\n<p>Love you all. I appreciate everything you do, and I\u2019m grateful to walk this journey with you.</p>\n<p><em><strong>Together through Christ  we have endless potential.</strong></em></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 10, "score_up": 40, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToZ25lBs", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 44, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "reeee", "id": 8927314,